# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Line endings: LF in the index and in every checkout.
#
# The index side is already there — 395 of the 406 tracked files are LF — but
# nothing pins the checkout side, so the working tree depends on the cloner's
# `core.autocrlf`: on a Windows box with the Git for Windows default (`true`) 89
# files land CRLF, 3 more land with both endings inside one file, and the same
# commit therefore hands two developers differently-shaped sources. Every tool
# that reads bytes and writes bytes back — rustfmt, a patch fixture, a
# `\r`-sensitive test — then behaves differently for each of them.
#
# This changes no tracked byte: for every file the rule below touches the index
# already holds LF, so only a fresh checkout sees a difference.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
* text=auto eol=lf

# Not text at all: certificate fixtures and the window icon are opaque bytes,
# never normalized and never merged line-wise.
crates/dpi-core/src/net/testdata/*.der -text
crates/dpi-detector/assets/*.ico -text
